WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:01.550
Hey, David.

00:00:01.550 --> 00:00:06.250
I'm looking at the electoral map, and it just
doesn't seem like Trump can win.

00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:10.710
Is it even possible for Trump to get 270 electoral
votes at this point?

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:12.960
Yes, yes, yes, yes, yes.

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:18.949
Do not for a fraction of a second think that
there is not a path to victory for Donald

00:00:18.949 --> 00:00:19.949
Trump.

00:00:19.949 --> 00:00:21.289
There is a path to victory for Donald Trump.

00:00:21.289 --> 00:00:23.730
Now, I understand the thought process.

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:30.720
If you start with the 2016 map and you look
at, wow, Trump lost the popular vote by three

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:31.720
million.

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:37.789
And it was really one of the narrowest scenarios
where you could lose nationally by three million

00:00:37.789 --> 00:00:39.120
and win electorally.

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:43.340
And the reason Trump won was because of three
states, Michigan.

00:00:43.340 --> 00:00:45.730
Trump won by like zero point two percent.

00:00:45.730 --> 00:00:49.109
It was a ten thousand vote margin in Michigan.

00:00:49.109 --> 00:00:53.579
In Pennsylvania, Trump won by under one point.

00:00:53.579 --> 00:00:56.899
And in Wisconsin, Trump won by under one point.

00:00:56.899 --> 00:01:02.800
It was only about 23000 votes, 22000 something
votes in Wisconsin.

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:07.660
So when you look at that and you say, well,
OK.

00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:10.140
That's how it was in 2016.

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:12.100
Trump's losing Wisconsin.

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:13.850
He's losing Michigan.

00:01:13.850 --> 00:01:15.620
He's losing Arizona, which he won.

00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:17.450
He's losing Florida, which he won.

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:19.220
He's only winning by one in Georgia.

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:21.170
He's only winning by two in Texas.

00:01:21.170 --> 00:01:23.570
North Carolina is basically a tie.

00:01:23.570 --> 00:01:25.540
Ohio is basically a tie.

00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:27.530
Iowa's barely in the Trump camp.

00:01:27.530 --> 00:01:28.530
Right.

00:01:28.530 --> 00:01:32.140
So when you look at it, you just say Biden's
going to flip something.

00:01:32.140 --> 00:01:33.140
Biden's going to flip something.

00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:38.010
And then immediately, the map becomes very
difficult for Donald Trump.

00:01:38.010 --> 00:01:40.510
Do not fall into that line of thinking.

00:01:40.510 --> 00:01:44.870
It is very much the case that Donald Trump
has a small margin of error.

00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:48.350
He can't afford to lose very much and still
win.

00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:54.060
And I think it's important to remember how
traumatized we are by 2016.

00:01:54.060 --> 00:02:00.230
And that may make some of us find paths for
Trump in order to not get a false sense of

00:02:00.230 --> 00:02:01.420
security.

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:04.140
You don't need to concoct anything outrageous.

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:10.010
What you have to remember is Donald Trump
is a desperate, cornered animal.

00:02:10.010 --> 00:02:16.521
We learned earlier this week that Don Junior
reportedly fears that if Trump loses, they

00:02:16.521 --> 00:02:18.670
all get prosecuted and indicted.

00:02:18.670 --> 00:02:23.660
So Trump is fighting not only for his political
life here, but he's fighting at least has

00:02:23.660 --> 00:02:29.810
done far, as Don Junior thinks, to keep himself
out of court potentially for the next however

00:02:29.810 --> 00:02:30.810
many years.

00:02:30.810 --> 00:02:33.830
But he lives, quite frankly, I don't necessarily
believe that.

00:02:33.830 --> 00:02:37.930
But if you believe Don Junior believes it,
they are acting out of desperation.

00:02:37.930 --> 00:02:40.170
So they're going to do post office.

00:02:40.170 --> 00:02:42.490
They're going to do voter suppression.

00:02:42.490 --> 00:02:46.280
They're going to allow foreign meddling, which
they've never tried to stop bill after bill

00:02:46.280 --> 00:02:48.010
after bill over the last four years.

00:02:48.010 --> 00:02:49.670
Mitch McConnell does nothing with it.

00:02:49.670 --> 00:02:52.450
Trump never talks about, you know, OK, you
get it.

00:02:52.450 --> 00:02:54.260
Purging voter rolls.

00:02:54.260 --> 00:02:55.620
They're going to do all of it.

00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:57.590
So I get it.

00:02:57.590 --> 00:03:02.270
You look at the map from 2016 and you go,
well, if you just flip Florida, I mean, it's

00:03:02.270 --> 00:03:03.760
already looking bad for Trump.

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:06.080
If you just flip Wisconsin and Pennsylvania.

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:07.920
But I get it.

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:08.920
Do not.

00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:12.650
We don't need to pretend that Trump is winning
by a lot right now.

00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:17.040
We just need to understand that you could,
again, have Joe Biden win.

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:21.430
Maybe Biden wins instead of by three million
votes, by four million votes.

00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:24.660
But that extra million comes in blue states.

00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:28.000
And Trump still pulls off an electoral victory.

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:29.960
That's the way we have to be thinking.

00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:34.830
And yes, Donald Trump very much can achieve
270 electoral votes

